NAME
    mount - list or activate configured volumes

SYNOPSIS
    mount
    mount VOLUME

DESCRIPTION
    With no arguments, lists every entry from the boot volume policy, its
    /vol path, filesystem, access mode, activation mode, and current state.

    With VOLUME, activates a validated entry configured with
    activation = "manual". The command cannot select arbitrary devices,
    filesystems, or paths; all stable identities and authority come from the
    boot policy. Already-mounted volumes succeed without changing state.
